{"id": "unknown-2026-08-28-010", "date": "2026-08-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak", "uncertainty"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Investments in co-located solar-plus-storage reach $25 billion in H1, says BloombergNEF", "content": "<p>Global renewable energy investment reached $327.5 billion in the first half of 2026, as capital shifted toward solar-plus-storage projects amid growing revenue uncertainty. US investment surged ahead of tax credit deadlines, while weaker activity in China and offshore wind weighed on the global outlook.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/investments-in-co-located-solar-plus-storage-reach-25-billion-in-h1-says-bloombergnef/\">Investments in co-located solar-plus-sto", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/investments-in-co-located-solar-plus-storage-reach-25-billion-in-h1-says-bloombergnef/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-28-011", "date": "2026-08-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The Hydrogen Stream: Africa’s first PV-driven hydrogen hub powers up", "content": "<p>Cbm-Tech has launched a green hydrogen hub in Walvis Bay combining 5 MW of solar, a 5 MW PEM electrolyzer and 5.9 MWh of battery storage.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/the-hydrogen-stream-africas-first-full-stack-pv-driven-hydrogen-hub-powers-up-in-namibia/\">The Hydrogen Stream: Africa’s first PV-driven hydrogen hub powers up</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/the-hydrogen-stream-africas-first-full-stack-pv-driven-hydrogen-hub-powers-up-in-namibia/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-28-012", "date": "2026-08-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Wood Mackenzie raises Latin America storage forecast to 34 GW by 2035", "content": "<p>Wood Mackenzie forecasts Latin America’s energy storage capacity to surge from 2.5 GW in 2025 to 34 GW by 2035, driven by renewable curtailment, grid constraints, auctions, and supportive policies. Chile leads deployment, while Mexico, Brazil, Argentina, and the Dominican Republic are scaling up, though unclear revenue models, financing constraints, and regulatory gaps remain key barriers.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/wood-mackenzie-raises-latin-america-stor", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/wood-mackenzie-raises-latin-america-storage-forecast-to-34-gw-by-2035/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-28-013", "date": "2026-08-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["trade_tariff", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["uncertainty"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Canada’s solar sector sees growing momentum across differing provincial markets", "content": "<p>While Canada’s provinces and territories continue to prioritise solar to different degrees, US tariff uncertainty is reinforcing national-level plans to invest in renewables and more integrated energy infrastructure.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/canadas-solar-sector-sees-growing-momentum-across-differing-provincial-markets/\">Canada’s solar sector sees growing momentum across differing provincial markets</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/canadas-solar-sector-sees-growing-momentum-across-differing-provincial-markets/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-28-014", "date": "2026-08-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Europe’s solar resource surplus continues before late-August cloud shift", "content": "<p>In a new weekly update for <b>pv magazine</b>, Solcast, a DNV company, reports that Europe’s solar irradiance averaged 5% above the 2007–2025 norm in August 2026, with nearly three-quarters of the continent seeing above-average levels due to persistent high pressure and clear skies. Conditions shifted later in the month as cooler, cloudier weather reduced gains in western Europe, while central and eastern regions retained much of their irradiance surplus.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/europes-solar-resource-surplus-continues-before-late-august-cloud-shift/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "array-2026-08-28-015", "date": "2026-08-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["array"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Machine learning improves irradiance prediction in bifacial PV systems", "content": "<p>A Selçuk University researcher has compared six machine learning algorithms for predicting front- and rear-side plane-of-array irradiance in bifacial PV systems. Random forest delivered the best results for both sides, while rear-side irradiance proved more difficult to predict.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/machine-learning-improves-irradiance-prediction-in-bifacial-pv-systems/\">Machine learning improves irradiance prediction in bifacial PV systems</a> appea", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/machine-learning-improves-irradiance-prediction-in-bifacial-pv-systems/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-28-016", "date": "2026-08-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["overcapacity"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Why China is struggling to consolidate its PV industry", "content": "<p><b>pv magazine</b> spoke with Alexander Brown, Senior Analyst at the Mercator Institute for China Studies (MERICS), about why consolidation in China’s PV industry is taking longer than expected, how the current downturn differs from previous overcapacity cycles, and why intense competition, technological change and local government support are making it difficult to remove excess manufacturing capacity.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/why-china-is-struggling-to", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/why-china-is-struggling-to-consolidate-its-pv-industry/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-28-017", "date": "2026-08-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["module_price", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["leading", "loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Chinese PV Industry Brief: Leading solar manufacturers report H1 losses", "content": "<p>Persistent oversupply and low module prices continue to weigh on the profitability of China’s leading PV manufacturers.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/chinese-pv-industry-brief-leading-pv-manufacturers-report-h1-losses/\">Chinese PV Industry Brief: Leading solar manufacturers report H1 losses</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/chinese-pv-industry-brief-leading-pv-manufacturers-report-h1-losses/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-28-018", "date": "2026-08-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Global PV additions forecast to reach 638 GW in 2026", "content": "<p>Analysis by Intertek CEA adds that structural oversupply is severe and persistent, with manufacturing capacity across all stages exceeding projected 2026 demand by wide margins.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/global-pv-additions-forecast-to-reach-638-gw-in-2026/\">Global PV additions forecast to reach 638 GW in 2026 </a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/28/global-pv-additions-forecast-to-reach-638-gw-in-2026/", "type": "rss"}]}
